The simplest mental model is:
    SharePoint List ≈ Dataverse Table

In SharePoint, the main object is simply a List. You can create it in different ways:
        Blank list → build your own columns, similar to creating a Dataverse custom table.
        From a template → for scenarios like issue tracking, work progress, etc.
        From an existing list → copy the structure.
        From Excel/CSV → create a list based on existing tabular data.
But these don't become fundamentally different table types like Activity Table vs Standard Table in Dataverse.
